  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Cab's Papers and the Meter Slip",
    "overview": "Two surfaces share one yellow and nothing else ornamental. The operator pages (`features/platform/**`) read like a licensed cab's papers: identifiers set like plates, counts in tabular slashed-zero figures, every trip's stage on a five-segment rail, flat underline tabs whose current tab burns with a deeper yellow rule. The rider pages (`features/storefront/**`) read like getting a meter slip on the kerb at night: asphalt ground, kerb-stone panels, the fare in big wide figures on a signal-yellow slip, and one signal-yellow action.\n\nBoth worlds are square and dense. Corners stay between 1px and 6px; the yellow is a spot colour reserved for the one action that moves work forward, the current tab or chosen option, and (rider side) the quote slip. Operator pages follow the shared dashboard shell's light and dark neutrals and add their own plate tokens; rider pages are always dark (`.rs.dark` scope). The shared dashboard shell (`features/dashboard/**`) is not part of this system and keeps its own tokens.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Spot yellow only: cab yellow on operator pages, signal yellow on rider pages, never as decoration.",
      "Square geometry: 1px status marks, 3px plates and rider controls, 4px operator controls, 6px panels and rows.",
      "Figures are instruments: tabular, slashed-zero counts and times; wide Archivo for rider fares and headings.",
      "Routes drawn as two stops on a rail: ring for pickup, solid square for drop-off.",
      "Flat operator surfaces; the rider booking panel alone lifts off the asphalt."
